RISC-V: Math.BigMul(ulong, ulong, out ulong) as mul + mulhu. Applied after perf-43; JIT and CoreLib.
- RV64M has mulhu, but Math.BigMul only special-cases x64 and arm64, so on RISC-V every 64x64->128
  multiply runs the out-of-line Hacker's Delight fallback (four 32x32 multiplies plus the carries), and
  UInt128 and Int128 multiplication with it.
- CoreLib: Math.BigMul(ulong, ulong, out ulong) becomes [Intrinsic]. Other targets do not expand it, so
  it stays an ordinary call there.
- JIT: on RISC-V the importer expands it into a mul of the factors stored through the out parameter and
  a GT_INTRINSIC (NI_System_Math_BigMul) for the high half, which codegen emits as mulhu (GT_MULHI is not
  valid in HIR). The factors are spilled to temps first, so "BigMul(a, b, out a)" still multiplies the
  original a and evaluation order (factors, then the address) is kept. VN gives the high half its own
  commutative function (VNF_MulHi_UN), so repeated products CSE.

